  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-3,0],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-3)$ and $f(0)$ inclusively.\n\nSince $f(-3)=-1$ and $f(0)=1$, we must have \n$k\\in [-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$-1$ and $1$\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062906/assets/50f937db1a3a87b1887eb22851b285190f1a8999c986af7f1cf32a1676873da2.png)",
